<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for March 19.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for March 19.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, on Tuesday published the following forecasts and data for gas consumption in the period March 17-19.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Mar 17 (actual) 213 mcm, 50 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 18 (forecast) 240 mcm, 56 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 19 (forecast) 256 mcm, 60 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Mar 17 (actual) 10.6 Celsius, seasonal normal 6.5 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 18 (forecast) 8.3 Celsius, seasonal normal 6.6 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 19 (forecast) 7.0 Celsius, seasonal normal 6.7 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption on Tuesday, and none expected on Wednesday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
